# ARAB Site (`arab/`)

Laravel 11 + Blade + Livewire 3 + Tailwind CSS 4. Locales: **`ar` + `en`**, default RTL for `ar`.

## Design

- Palette: gold, emerald, white/sand, black/ink (wealth, Islam, prestige).
- Fonts: **Cairo**, **Tajawal**, **Almarai** (Arabic) + **Montserrat**, **Poppins** (Latin). English uses Poppins/Montserrat first.
- Visual: minimalism with Islamic geometry, arabesque/calligraphy ornaments, abstract blockchain nodes. No Qur’anic verses as decoration.
- Hero: full-bleed, brand-first; one headline, one supporting line, one CTA group.
- No inset/card hero media; no floating badges/overlays on hero.
- Prefer motion for hierarchy (2–3 intentional motions), not clutter.

## Imagery

- Prefer: modest traditional dress, Dubai/Doha skylines, abstract chain visuals.
- Never: pigs, alcohol, revealing clothing, idols or symbols that contradict Islam.

## Product / UX specifics

- Section **Sharia** (compliance angle for MENA); WhatsApp as primary messenger CTA.
- Investment calculator: **USD / AED / SAR / QAR**; price & FX from Hub settings (fallback `config/site.php`).
- Testimonials allowed; keep first viewport free of stats/schedules/extra promo blocks.

## Content & Hub

- `site_key`: `arab`. Fetch via `HubClient`; never hardcode Hub URLs in views.
- Site overrides in Hub may differ from CHINA (Sharia vs Tech Stack, messengers, copy).
- On Hub outage: render from `config/site.php` fallback; still queue leads/events for retry.

## Do not

- Copy CHINA WeChat/QR or CNY-only UX into ARAB.
- Put ICO/crypto compliance workarounds meant for China into ARAB public copy without product ask.
